sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Client as Client / Browser
    participant Server as Express Server
    participant DB as PostgreSQL Database

    Note over Client, DB: 1. Login Flow
    Client->>+Server: POST /api/v1/auth/login (email/username, password)
    Server->>+DB: Find user by email/username
    DB-->>-Server: User record with passwordHash
    Server->>Server: Verify password with Argon2
    Server->>Server: Generate sessionId (UUID) & refreshToken (JWT)
    Server->>Server: Generate SHA-256 hash of refreshToken
    Server->>+DB: INSERT Session (id=sessionId, refreshTokenHash, expiresAt, ip, userAgent)
    DB-->>-Server: Session created
    Server->>Server: Generate accessToken (JWT with userId)
    Server-->>-Client: 200 OK (JSON user data)<br/>Set-Cookie: accessToken (HttpOnly, Path: /)<br/>Set-Cookie: refreshToken (HttpOnly, Path: /auth)

    Note over Client, DB: 2. Authenticated Protected Route Request
    Client->>+Server: GET /api/v1/users/me<br/>Cookie: accessToken=...
    Server->>Server: authenticate middleware: Verify JWT signature & expiry
    Server->>+DB: Find user by userId (sub)
    DB-->>-Server: User record
    Server-->>-Client: 200 OK (Protected User Profile Data)

    Note over Client, DB: 3. Token Refresh & Rotation Flow
    Client->>+Server: POST /api/v1/auth/refresh<br/>Cookie: refreshToken=...
    Server->>Server: verifyRefreshToken: Decode token, get userId and sessionId (sid)
    Server->>Server: Compute SHA-256 hash of incoming refreshToken
    Server->>+DB: Fetch Session by sessionId
    DB-->>-Server: Stored session record
    Server->>Server: Check if session revoked or expired
    Server->>Server: Generate newRefreshToken & new accessToken
    Server->>Server: Compute SHA-256 hash of newRefreshToken
    Server->>+DB: UPDATE Session WHERE id=sessionId AND refreshTokenHash=oldHash<br/>SET refreshTokenHash=newHash, lastUsedAt=now, expiresAt=newExpiresAt
    DB-->>-Server: Update result (count: 1)
    Server-->>-Client: 200 OK<br/>Set-Cookie: accessToken (HttpOnly, Path: /)<br/>Set-Cookie: refreshToken (HttpOnly, Path: /auth)

    Note over Client, DB: 4. Logout Flow
    Client->>+Server: POST /api/v1/auth/logout<br/>Cookie: refreshToken=...
    Server->>Server: Decode refreshToken to extract sessionId
    Server->>+DB: UPDATE Session SET revokedAt=NOW() WHERE id=sessionId
    DB-->>-Server: Session revoked
    Server-->>-Client: 200 OK<br/>Clear-Cookie: accessToken (Path: /)<br/>Clear-Cookie: refreshToken (Path: /auth)
